# NOTE: the data patterns below are ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose.
# An unanchored `context/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which
# silently excluded the entire src/personalagi/context/ source package from
# every commit. Anchor anything that names a top-level data directory.
/credentials/
/tokens/
.env
*.db
__pycache__/
.venv/

# The vault: real names, addresses, and private correspondence. Never committed.
# See context.example/ for the structure.
/context/

# Derived artifacts — rebuildable from context/ by reindexing.
/data/

# Rendered briefs summarise private correspondence.
/briefs/

# Eval CSVs quote real messages — subjects, body excerpts, sender addresses.
# Matched by extension, not by filename: the previous version named
# labels.csv and labels_template.csv individually, so labels_v2_template.csv
# was about to be committed. Enumerating files you must not commit is the same
# class of mistake as an unanchored pattern — it fails silently and looks fine.
# Markdown in evals/ (TAXONOMY.md, RESULTS.md) is tracked on purpose.
/evals/*.csv

# Python / tooling
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# macOS
.DS_Store
